<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:AgIO.Views"
        x:Class="AgIO.Views.FormEthernet"
        x:DataType="vm:FormEthernetViewModel"
        Title="Ethernet Configuration"
        RequestedThemeVariant="Light"
        Width="800" Height="340"
        CanResize="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        SystemDecorations="Full"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="14">
    <!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms FormEthernet.cs + FormEthernet.designer.cs — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
    <!--
        [XPLAT] Avalonia 1:1 PARITY reimplementation of the deleted WinForms AgIO "Ethernet"
        loopback-config dialog (Forms/FormEthernet.Designer.cs + Forms/FormEthernet.cs). This dialog
        sets the four bytes of the UDP loopback address AgIO uses to reach AgOpenGPS over the local
        loopback fabric, plus the master "UDP on" flag. NO redesign (AAP §0.3.3) — the layout mirrors
        the WinForms designer exactly.

        Parity mapping to FormEthernet.Designer.cs:
          • Form Text "Ethernet Configuration"  -> Title="Ethernet Configuration".
          • ClientSize 772 x 254 / FixedDialog   -> compact fixed Width=800 Height=340, CanResize="False"
                                                    (the WinForms form had FormBorderStyle.FixedDialog
                                                    and ControlBox=false — a fixed footprint).
          • StartPosition CenterParent           -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner".
          • ShowInTaskbar = false                -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
          • Form Font Tahoma                     -> FontFamily="Tahoma".
          • groupBox3 Text "Linux Only !"        -> the titled Border on the left (header TextBlock).
          • nudFirstIP=127 . nudSecndIP=255 .    -> four NumericUpDown octets (0..255, increment 1) in a
            nudThirdIP=255 . nudFourthIP=255        horizontal row, separated by "." TextBlocks, reading
            (label2/label3/label1 were the dots)    like the dotted-quad loopback address.
          • cboxIsUDPOn "UDP Is On/Off" toggle   -> CheckBox x:Name="cboxIsUDPOn" Content="UDP On".
          • label4 "Turn UDP On And Hit OK"      -> the hint TextBlock above the checkbox.
          • btnSerialCancel (carried OK64, was   -> split per the agent-prompt into an explicit
            the SAVE action) + Program.Restart()    btnSerialOK (accept/save) and btnSerialCancel
                                                    (dismiss), in the bottom command bar.

        Bound to FormEthernetViewModel via COMPILED bindings (x:DataType above):
          • The four octets TwoWay-bind to LoopOne / LoopTwo / LoopThree / LoopFour (held as int by the
            view-model precisely so they bind cleanly to the numeric editors / on-screen keypad; the
            (byte) narrowing and the 0..255 clamp live in the view-model).
          • The check box TwoWay-binds to IsUdpOn.
          • OK/Cancel bind to SaveCommand / CancelCommand (RelayCommand). SaveCommand persists the bytes
            + flag, then raises RequestConfirm / RequestRestart / RequestClose; CancelCommand raises
            RequestClose without persisting. Those events are handled by the hosting window's code-behind
            (FormEthernet.axaml.cs) — they are NOT a XAML concern.

        On-screen numeric keypad: the former NumericUpDown.ShowKeypad(this) tap-to-edit behaviour is
        presented by the code-behind via the Controls/NumericUpDownExtensions.ShowKeypad helper, which
        finds these editors by their x:Name. The view therefore declares NO event attributes, staying
        fully decoupled from that wiring (mirrors the sibling FormRadioChannel / FormSource convention).

        Buttons render as TEXT, not the WinForms OK64 / Cancel64 bitmaps: the migrated AgIO.csproj
        registers NO btnImages assets as <AvaloniaResource> (only GPS/AgOpenGPS.csproj does) and excludes
        Properties/Resources.Designer.cs from compilation (System.Drawing purged). Referencing
        avares://AgIO/btnImages/* here would not resolve and would render a broken image, so every
        migrated AgIO view uses text affordances — consistent with the documented convention in the
        sibling FormSource.axaml / FormRadioChannel.axaml / FormYes.axaml. See MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md.

        Theme: Light only — App.axaml pins RequestedThemeVariant="Light" (AgIO has no day/night toggle);
        it is restated on the window for explicitness/parity, mirroring the sibling AgIO views.
    -->
    <Grid Margin="20" RowDefinitions="*,Auto" RowSpacing="16">

        <!-- Row 0 — top content: the loopback-octet group (left) and the UDP toggle + hint (right). -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="24">

            <!--
                WinForms groupBox3 "Linux Only !" — a titled frame around the four octet editors.
                Avalonia has no GroupBox primitive, so a Border + header TextBlock reproduces the look.
            -->
            <Border Grid.Column="0"
                    BorderBrush="#40000000"
                    BorderThickness="1"
                    CornerRadius="4"
                    Padding="16,10,16,16"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <StackPanel Spacing="8">

                    <!-- groupBox3.Text "Linux Only !" (Tahoma 15.75 Bold). -->
                    <TextBlock Text="Linux Only !"
                               FontSize="16"
                               FontWeight="Bold" />

                    <!--
                        The four loopback octets, separated by "." so the row reads as a dotted-quad
                        address. Each editor is large and centre-aligned for touch (Phase 3). The
                        spinner is shown but spin is disabled — the primary input is the on-screen
                        keypad wired by the code-behind, exactly like the WinForms original which
                        disabled the editable up/down box and used ShowKeypad.
                    -->
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                                VerticalAlignment="Center">

                        <!-- nudFirstIP -> LoopOne (WinForms default 127). -->
                        <NumericUpDown x:Name="nudFirstIP"
                                       Width="118" Height="62"
                                       Minimum="0" Maximum="255" Increment="1"
                                       Value="{Binding LoopOne, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       FormatString="0"
                                       ClipValueToMinMax="True"
                                       ShowButtonSpinner="True"
                                       AllowSpin="False"
                                       TextAlignment="Center"
                                       HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                       VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                                       FontSize="22" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       AutomationProperties.Name="Loopback address octet 1" />

                        <TextBlock Text="."
                                   FontSize="28" FontWeight="Bold"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                   Margin="4,0" />

                        <!-- nudSecndIP -> LoopTwo. -->
                        <NumericUpDown x:Name="nudSecndIP"
                                       Width="118" Height="62"
                                       Minimum="0" Maximum="255" Increment="1"
                                       Value="{Binding LoopTwo, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       FormatString="0"
                                       ClipValueToMinMax="True"
                                       ShowButtonSpinner="True"
                                       AllowSpin="False"
                                       TextAlignment="Center"
                                       HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                       VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                                       FontSize="22" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       AutomationProperties.Name="Loopback address octet 2" />

                        <TextBlock Text="."
                                   FontSize="28" FontWeight="Bold"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                   Margin="4,0" />

                        <!-- nudThirdIP -> LoopThree. -->
                        <NumericUpDown x:Name="nudThirdIP"
                                       Width="118" Height="62"
                                       Minimum="0" Maximum="255" Increment="1"
                                       Value="{Binding LoopThree, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       FormatString="0"
                                       ClipValueToMinMax="True"
                                       ShowButtonSpinner="True"
                                       AllowSpin="False"
                                       TextAlignment="Center"
                                       HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                       VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                                       FontSize="22" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       AutomationProperties.Name="Loopback address octet 3" />

                        <TextBlock Text="."
                                   FontSize="28" FontWeight="Bold"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                   Margin="4,0" />

                        <!-- nudFourthIP -> LoopFour. -->
                        <NumericUpDown x:Name="nudFourthIP"
                                       Width="118" Height="62"
                                       Minimum="0" Maximum="255" Increment="1"
                                       Value="{Binding LoopFour, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       FormatString="0"
                                       ClipValueToMinMax="True"
                                       ShowButtonSpinner="True"
                                       AllowSpin="False"
                                       TextAlignment="Center"
                                       HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                       VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                                       FontSize="22" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       AutomationProperties.Name="Loopback address octet 4" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>

            <!-- Right group — the WinForms label4 hint stacked above the cboxIsUDPOn toggle. -->
            <StackPanel Grid.Column="1"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="12">

                <!-- label4 "Turn UDP On And Hit OK" (Tahoma 14.25 Bold), centred over the toggle. -->
                <TextBlock Text="Turn UDP On And Hit OK"
                           FontSize="15"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           TextAlignment="Center"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           MaxWidth="200" />

                <!--
                    cboxIsUDPOn -> IsUdpOn. The WinForms control was a button-appearance check box that
                    toggled its caption between "UDP Is On"/"UDP Is Off"; the view-model exposes only the
                    boolean IsUdpOn, so this is a large touch-friendly CheckBox whose checked state is the
                    on/off indicator. Kept as a CheckBox (not a ToggleButton) to match the x:Name contract.
                -->
                <CheckBox x:Name="cboxIsUDPOn"
                          Content="UDP On"
                          IsChecked="{Binding IsUdpOn, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          MinHeight="56"
                          Padding="14,8"
                          FontSize="18"
                          FontWeight="Bold"
                          HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                          VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                          AutomationProperties.Name="UDP networking on" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Grid>

        <!--
            Row 1 — command bar. Cancel sits to the LEFT of OK so OK (the accept action) stays
            right-aligned, mirroring the sibling AgIO views. OK = SaveCommand (persist + confirm +
            restart + close); Cancel = CancelCommand (dismiss without persisting).
        -->
        <StackPanel Grid.Row="1"
                    Orientation="Horizontal"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                    VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                    Spacing="12">

            <!-- WinForms btnSerialCancel (dismiss). IsCancel maps Escape to this command. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnSerialCancel"
                    Content="Cancel"
                    Command="{Binding CancelCommand}"
                    IsCancel="True"
                    Width="101" Height="64"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Close without saving"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel" />

            <!-- WinForms btnSerialCancel/OK64 accept action -> btnSerialOK. IsDefault maps Enter to OK. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnSerialOK"
                    Content="OK"
                    Command="{Binding SaveCommand}"
                    IsDefault="True"
                    Width="101" Height="64"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Save the loopback configuration and restart AgIO"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="OK" />
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</Window>
